                  <provenance cert="low" source="1228"><orgName role="fmo" key="mlgbOrg_4">Canterbury, Kent. Benedictine
                        cathedral priory of Holy Trinity or Christ Church</orgName><p>Zigzag, with
                        a dot on the head- and base-line (fol. 1r).</p><p>Said by M. R. James (Anc.
                        Libr., p. xciii) to be in the Christ Church hand of the 12th century and to
                        be identified also by its mark on fol. 1r. It is not in the Christ Church
                        catalogues, but is in the Dover catalogue (late 14th century) and bears the
                        Dover pressmark.</p></provenance>
                  <provenance type="MLGB3_laterOwners">J. Joscelin</provenance>
               <provenance source="1918"><orgName role="fmo" key="mlgbOrg_3">Dover, Kent. Benedictine priory of
                        St Mary the Virgin and St Martin; cell of Canterbury cathedral priory</orgName><p>'D [enclosing:] 4 : VII : Vita sancti Dunstani .... Regnante
                        magnifico .... 81 . . . 4..', s. xiv (foot of fol. 2r): 'D4 VII' is the
                        distinctio and gradus; 'Vita sancti Dunstani' is the first item in the
                        volume; 'regnante magnifico' are the first words of fol. 2r; '81' is the
                        number of leaves; and '4' is the number of works in the volume.</p><p>' ...
                        is written in the Christ Church hand of the twelfth centuury, and has,
                        besides, a mark on the upper corner of its first leaf [cf. Digby 13] which
                        shows that it must once have stood on the Christ Church shelves' (James,
                        ALCD, p. xciii) = no. 167 in the Dover catalogue (James, ALCD, p. 421). Not
                        in Christ Church catalogues.</p><q type="pressmark">D.VII.4</q></provenance>
                  </history>
